{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788116137,"nonce":"gqMFjo77aFkinbov+8QhLjD9MaQ=","message":"AMENDMENT from spike 0.1 (FINDINGS.md, git-bug 3fa4cf5) — orchestrator, post-gate.\n\nThree findings bear on the journal. Scope and Acceptance stand.\n\n**Letters open once per FRAME, not once per tick — read the stack, not the UI.**\n`Game.UpdatePlay` calls `Find.LetterStack.OpenAutomaticLetters()` exactly once\nper frame, before `TickManagerUpdate`. Under fast-forward the advance loop runs\nhundreds of ticks per frame (vanilla itself runs up to 300), so several letters\ncan accumulate in the stack before the first one opens. Capture letters from\n`LetterStack` state, never from an opened-dialog side effect, or a burst will\njournal one letter and drop the rest. This is also why 1.3's `advance\nuntil:letter` must consult the stack directly — flagged there too.\n\n**Alerts trail the tick that caused them.** Alerts are recomputed by\n`UIRootUpdate` on its own cadence, so an alert-derived event lands a frame or\ntwo after the state change that triggered it. Combined with DESIGN's standing\npoint that alerts fire LATE by design (tattered-apparel means the mood penalty\nalready landed), an `alert_on` event's `gameTick` is \"when the readout noticed\",\nnot \"when it became true\". Worth saying so in the schema doc, since 5.1 will\nassert on these.\n\n**The bench's known-benign warning set is 9, and it repeats every boot.** Spike\nboots landed 0 errors / 9 warnings, reproduced independently by the orchestrator\non a clean boot: SteamAPI.Init failure x1 (by design — the bench detaches\nSteam), Guests Socio-Butterfly degradation x2 (deferred-tier mod absent),\nStaticConstructorOnStartup hygiene notes x6 (Guests x3, FSWA x2,\nRealisticGasses x1 — these appear only because devMode=True is seeded). Full\ntriage in FINDINGS section 5. This is the concrete input to this spec's\n\"warning (deduped)\" open question: dedupe policy should make these nine cost\nnine journal lines per session, not nine per scan.","files":null}]}